    "progressSummary": "COMPLETED: snf_1x2_invariant_factor_pid proved for any GCDMonoid. New gallery entry created. 2 axioms (snf_pid_exists, snf_pid_solvability). 0 sorries.",
    "builtItems": [
      "Proved snf_1x2_invariant_factor (BezoutIdentityOQ04OQ01.lean)",
      "Created BezoutIdentityOQ04OQ01OQ01.lean: PID generalization of BezoutIdentityOQ04OQ01",
      "Proved snf_1x2_invariant_factor_pid for any CommRing/IsDomain/GCDMonoid",
      "Created src/data/proofs/bezout-identity-oq-04-oq-01-oq-01/ gallery entry"
    ],
    "insights": [
      "Mathlib has Basis.SmithNormalForm and Submodule.smithNormalForm in LinearAlgebra.FreeModule.PID",
      "Parent proof uses custom axioms for SNF existence and solvability. These could potentially be replaced by Mathlib SNF.",
      "Generalization to PIDs: replace \u2124 with R [IsPrincipalIdealRing R] and use GCDMonoid/EuclideanDomain API",
      "snf_1x2_invariant_factor: d|gcd(a,b) because a=u*d*V[0,0] and b=u*d*V[0,1] from A=U*D*V decomposition",
      "gcd(a,b)|d because det(V)=\u00b11 implies a*V[1,1]-b*V[1,0]=\u00b1u*d, so d is a linear combination of a,b",
      "Main Lean challenge: extracting (U*D*V)[0,j] entries for Fin 1/Fin 2 matrices via Matrix.mul_apply + Fin.sum_univ",
      "SNF 1x2 proof: A 0 j = u * d * V 0 j where u = U 0 0 (+-1) and d = D 0 0",
      "Part 1 (d|gcd): d|a and d|b since a = d*(u*V00), b = d*(u*V01), then Int.dvd_gcd",
      "Part 2 (gcd|d): det(V)=+-1 gives a*V11 - b*V10 = u*d*det(V) = +-d, then gcd|a and gcd|b gives gcd|d",
      "Key Lean tactics: congr_fun (congr_fun hsnf 0) j for entry extraction, Matrix.mul_apply + Fin.sum for expansion",
      "Proof uses entry extraction from A=UDV via congr_fun, det_fin_one/two, and Fin.sum_univ simplification",
      "Key new technique: unit.inv_val replaces \u00b11 case split for backward direction gcd|d",
      "Theorem holds in any GCDMonoid (not just IsPrincipalIdealRing)",
      "Associated d (uval*d) via witness uval; dvd_iff gives gcd|d from gcd|uval*d",
      "linear_combination h works for CommRing (vs linarith in parent which is \u2124-specific)"
    ],
